      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "WebDyne versions from 2.031 before 3.022 for Perl execute files with .psp anywhere in the name as Perl pages.\n\nWebDyne decides whether to run a requested file as a page by matching its name against WEBDYNE_PSP_EXT_RE, which has no end anchor.\n\nAn application that accepts uploads by checking only the final extension lets a remote attacker upload a file such as report.psp.pdf and run its embedded Perl by requesting it.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
